From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000034
Subject: [PATCH] population_vendor_lanefill: a mod sets how full its lanes get

With Fill: Lanes, how much of a lane fills before the next one opens is the
YAML's LaneFillPct, which a player can't change from the app. This lets a
mod's OnInit hand a setting to the engine, per VendorKey prefix, like the
other population_vendor_* commands. It does nothing unless a script calls it.

--- a/src/custom/script.inc
+++ b/src/custom/script.inc
@@ -527,3 +527,18 @@
 	script_pushint(st, 1);
 	return SCRIPT_CMD_SUCCESS;
 }
+
+/*==========================================
+ * population_vendor_lanefill("<prefix>", <percent>)
+ *   With Fill: Lanes, the share of a lane's usable cells the mod vendors
+ *   whose VendorKey starts with the prefix take before the next lane opens
+ *   (1-100), over their YAML LaneFillPct: lower leaves wider gaps between
+ *   stalls and spreads them over more lanes. 0 or less goes back to the YAML.
+ *
+ *   population_vendor_lanefill "my-mod/", callfunc("F_ModSetting", "my-mod", "density", 80);
+ *------------------------------------------*/
+BUILDIN_FUNC(population_vendor_lanefill)
+{
+	population_engine_set_mod_vendor_lane_fill(script_getstr(st, 2), script_getnum(st, 3));
+	return SCRIPT_CMD_SUCCESS;
+}
--- a/src/custom/script_def.inc
+++ b/src/custom/script_def.inc
@@ -36,3 +36,4 @@
 BUILDIN_DEF(population_whisper_event, "is"),
 BUILDIN_DEF(population_whisper, "is"),
 BUILDIN_DEF(population_lost_event, "is"),
+BUILDIN_DEF(population_vendor_lanefill, "si"),
